<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2595d20ee84f613552fa4b706a83fa3e140b1e1976992ca08d7da96e435a0811</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>From delivery driver to global fame: A Korean writer's journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23477d77a1d122d95feb97bc1daac3fb26482268f12670c0d5ec47322392bf6b</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757--a579002c20b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">You Yeong-Gwang's The Rainfall Market tells the story of a mysterious, hidden shop that only opens when it rains. For a debut novel by an unknown author, it was a massive success.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The homeless man living in front of a London mega-mansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6fc6c9ffd3f015d3857bdcad5e660adc01fdb2be4fddceacab7f0231f660536</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925--903398310f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anders Fernstedt lives in London without any money. The Swedish native has built a most unusual home under the porch of a house worth over €200 million. How did that happen?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228a88072373da80702232c535f3adf99f25af8fceb4111b30819e1da5ca3776</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db08b2188c296d6ebad867cb1799c3061c6f5c5d52f1abc60ba694f767fccc34</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15bc992553f8d6f6ba4824ce64e94482ce8e08280790398b48f50194cea87b4f</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b16cf1c739dd994df93a727f5c6f41d3770d42ae44909027406838723569f24c</id><updated>2026-10-24T18:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
